{
  "about": [
    "Query vectors for the trace tool.",
    "Authored in canopy (tests/canopy_mcp/fixtures/workspace/); every other holder keeps a byte-identical copy of the whole directory.",
    "ASCII-only, no trailing whitespace, exactly one final newline.",
    "Every query is copied verbatim from react-trace's query tests at d52a7b9 (test: '<describe> > <it>'); a query a test builds from constants or a template is written out as the string the test builds.",
    "verdict is what a command carrying the query as open_tool.query or set_query.query gets:",
    "invalid_command: the hub refuses the batch (the query is over 4096 UTF-8 bytes; the hub's only query bound).",
    "invalid_args: the viewer rejects the command (the tool's query grammar, its PV cap, or Trace's range).",
    "accepted: the command is applied; the tool's page falls back to its default for any key it cannot read.",
    "The viewer's rules: the query is decodable (every '&'-separated key and value survives decodeURIComponent); the distinct values of the tool's PV key (trace pv, correlation y, waveform pv; read as URLSearchParams does, '+' a space), blank ones not counted, number at most maxPvs.",
    "Trace: maxPvs 12; at least one key is pv or range; a range, when present, is one react-trace reads: -<n><m|h|d|w|M> or custom with a local from (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM[:SS], no zone), an optional to of the same form, from not after to."
  ],
  "tool": "trace",
  "source": "react-trace d52a7b9 src/embed/query.test.ts",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "preset literal",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > parses the preset literal",
      "query": "pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:01:POSITION:X&pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:02:POSITION:X&pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:03:POSITION:X&range=-1h",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "leading question mark",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > tolerates a leading \"?\"",
      "query": "?pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:01:POSITION:X&pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:02:POSITION:X&pv=XFER:DIAG:BPM:03:POSITION:X&range=-1h",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "url-encoded pv names",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > decodes URL-encoded PV names",
      "query": "pv=A%20B%26C&pv=D%3DE&range=-4h",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "relative range -30m",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > accepts any relative range resolveTimeWindow understands",
      "query": "pv=A&range=-30m",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "relative range -1.5h",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > accepts any relative range resolveTimeWindow understands",
      "query": "pv=A&range=-1.5h",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "relative range -2d",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > accepts any relative range resolveTimeWindow understands",
      "query": "pv=A&range=-2d",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "relative range -1w",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > accepts any relative range resolveTimeWindow understands",
      "query": "pv=A&range=-1w",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "relative range -1M",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > accepts any relative range resolveTimeWindow understands",
      "query": "pv=A&range=-1M",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "empty and whitespace pv names",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > skips empty and whitespace PV names",
      "query": "pv=&pv=%20%20&pv=A&pv=+&range=-1h",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "missing range",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > defaults a missing range to -1h without warning",
      "query": "pv=A",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "empty query",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > defaults a missing range to -1h without warning",
      "query": "",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "custom window with from and to",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > reads a custom window with from and to verbatim",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=2026-09-30T10:00&to=2026-09-30T11:30",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "custom window without to",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > reads a custom window without to as \"until now\"",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=2026-09-30T10:00",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "custom window with an empty to",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > treats an empty to as absent",
      "query": "range=custom&from=2026-09-30T10:00&to=",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "from on a relative range",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > ignores from/to on a relative range",
      "query": "range=-4h&from=2026-09-30T10:00",
      "verdict": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: unknown preset",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=yesterday",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: missing minus",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=1h",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: empty range",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: custom without from",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: custom with unparsable from",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=soon",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: custom with a zone",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=2026-09-30T10:00Z",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: custom with unparsable to",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=2026-09-30T10:00&to=later",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
    {
      "name": "bad range: custom with from after to",
      "test": "parseTraceQuery > bad range (%s) warns once and yields -1h",
      "query": "pv=A&range=custom&from=2026-09-30T12:00&to=2026-09-30T11:00",
      "verdict": "invalid_args"
    },
